## OUTPUT FORMAT

After invoking the required tool(s), emit a single combined report.

When OL Triage ran:
```
OL TRIAGE — Offer ID: {offer_id} | Store ID: {store_id}
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Listing Status:   {listing_status}
Overall Verdict:  {overall_verdict}
Matched Rule IDs: {matched_rule_ids}
Reason Codes:     {reason_codes}
Errors:           {errors}

Rendered Report (verbatim from DIAG-OL-RENDER-REPORT-01):
{report}
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
```

The ``{report}`` block carries the per-condition table with the real
``entry`` / ``operator`` / ``expected`` / ``actual`` values for every
matched rule — emit it verbatim, do NOT collapse it to ``conditionN``
identifiers.

When the unpublish validator ran:
```
UNPUBLISH VALIDATION — Offer ID: {offer_id}
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Publish Status:       {publish_status}
Audit History:        {audit_history}
Reason Codes Checked: {reason_codes_checked}

Per-Reason-Code Results:
{for each result}
  • {reason_code}: {status}
    Message: {message}
    Details: {details if non-empty}

Summary: {summary}
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Tool success: {success}
{if error: Error: {error}}
```

When ``check_mode == both``, emit BOTH blocks above, OL Triage first.

ONE diagnostic report, then STOP.
